    "created_at": "2016-10-04T12:55:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-04T12:55:30Z",
    "body": "Trying the test again, screenshots from Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari:\n\n![Chrome](https://www.browserstack.com/download?url=https://www.browserstack.com/issue-tracker/86fcf66c3e9a6faecf41ab043838489c228e72cd/win10_chrome_53.0.jpg)\n\n![Edge](https://www.browserstack.com/download?url=https://www.browserstack.com/issue-tracker/0cf5820ba117f5b752174cfd0a221ce6d8940c49/win10_edge_14.0.jpg)\n\n![Firefox](https://www.browserstack.com/download?url=https://www.browserstack.com/issue-tracker/2d3c5c062d2bd40ee1ff13a691aa8f848955d969/win10_firefox_48.0.jpg)\n\n![Safari](https://www.browserstack.com/download?url=https://www.browserstack.com/issue-tracker/2e214ab678879dcc9f307d1dc65662200efe69a6/macsie_safari_10.0.jpg)\n\nSo it's only Firefox that allows no nesting at all, while the rest have some weird stuff going on. Whether or not it's still required for web compat, spec'ing something like what Edge does seems reasonable.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
