    "created_at": "2026-10-17T07:44:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-17T07:44:57Z",
    "body": "I stumbled upon this due to WPT tests added as part of https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66 where https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/ca4621ae41d6c113c449ca60cf1a64897b27e167/dom/nodes/Document-base-url-not-live.window.js#L29 depends on this behaviour.\n\nstep 3 of the [shared attribute processing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#shared-attribute-processing-steps-for-iframe-and-frame-elements) also applies when url is about:blank.\n\nIf an iframe with no src/about:blank is inserted into an about:blank document, its URL matches an ancestor’s, so the steps return null. [Process the iframe attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#process-the-iframe-attributes) then returns before step 2.3, and the iframe never fires load (making that test time out).\n\nSo per current spec, that test should time out.\n\nBased on:\n- https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=251595\n- https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41088542\n\nLooks like at least chromium and webkit violate the spec here, webkit actually being changed this year for webcompat reasons.\n\nDoes sending a MR changing behaviour to skip about: URLs for this check seem reasonable I think it makes sense here.\n\ncc @noamr  @annevk ",
