    "created_at": "2026-10-18T00:53:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-18T00:53:55Z",
    "body": "Debugging a different test issue, I had one more finding that also happened to link to this issue. The guard in place for the shared attribute processing steps is not protected against for navigate. I believe the check should also be put in place for that to prevent unguarded recursion:\n\n```html\n<script>\nconst i = document.createElement(\"iframe\");\ndocument.body.append(i);\ni.contentWindow.location.href = location.href; // or navigation.navigate(\"#x\")\n</script>\n```\n\nI found this through this test: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/navigation-api/navigation-methods/return-value/navigate-initial-about-blank.html",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
